{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Strife, a brother</b> — two who are joined." "<b>offended</b> — on account of the offense that goes out from him he is so called, and the word <b>bar</b> [bolt] includes doors, and he mentioned it because they have no strength and might except with the bar, and <b>armon</b> [citadel] is a fortress, meaning: and between mighty and strong ones the [lot] will separate, so that they do not fight. And even if the brother be more offended than a fortified city, the offenders against their king — as in \"rebelled Libnah\" — and the strife of the brother be like the strength of the bar of a citadel, the lot will separate between them." "And he said <b>a brother</b> — because most quarrels are over the inheritance of brothers."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:35.831800246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}